> yet have a list but it will probably include car, effects, lme4 and
> r-cran-pbkrtest for instance, as they depend on r-cran-statmod.

Is r-cran-statmod a particularly troublesome package to build everywhere?
The autopkgtest results look good to me on s390x [1] and i386 [2], and
although there were some failures in the first half of 2024 on armhf
[3], they seem to have been good since then.

I don't think Dirk needs to modify any of his packages.  Firstly, car
and effects are architecture all, so adding Build-Depends on
architecture-is-64-bit and architecture-is-little-endian doesn't do
what you think it does.  This was raised on this list previously [4],
but I didn't see a response.  Secondly, if you do end up removing the
binaries of r-cran-statmod on some architectures, then lme4 and
r-cran-pbkrtest will no longer be able to build on those
architectures, and all you need to do is also request removal of the
binaries of lme4 and r-cran-pbkrtest.

Regards
Graham

