I continue to maintain that looking at CRAN should generally be enough. CRAN
has a field 'Deadline', not unlike our expulsion mechanism and I think both
those packages were under it.  But we can trust that when something comes to
CRAN then the package will

- build will all other CRAN packages
- build with current R ("r-release"), next R ("R-devel") and previous R ("R-oldrel")
- many packages also test against many more older versions

So I see no point in testing random permutations here, especially when it is
the same upstream team. The first step would just be to keep them all current.

Best, Dirk

